{"book":11,"chapter":8,"rubric":"MODERN FRONTEND / THE JAVASCRIPT LANGUAGE / CHAPTER 8","slides":[{"title":"Objects with behavior","sub":"Chapter 8 · From a literal to a class","short":"Intro","main":"Under classes lies the prototype chain.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Literal","Class","What is under it"],"captions":["Literals suit single objects, but many objects need shared behavior","JavaScript has classes for that — the syntax is familiar from Python and Java","Under a class lies its own model, the prototype chain; it explains inheritance and this"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["const u = {","  name: 'Ada',","  hi() { … },","};"],"lang":"js","size":11.0,"lh":20.0,"w":240.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["class User {","  constructor(name) {","    this.name = name;","  }","  hi() { … }","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":260.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"i","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"instance","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":146.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":214.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"prototype","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"every object links to a prototype","size":9.5}]],"cues":[14.0,33.7]}]},{"title":"Prototype chain","sub":"Lookup and shadowing","short":"Prototypes","main":"A field is looked up the chain; a write goes to the object itself.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Chain","Field lookup","Write and shadowing"],"captions":["Every object links to a prototype; the chain ends with the value null","A field is sought in the object, then up the chain: that is how toString is found in Object.prototype","A write always goes to the object itself, so an inherited value can be shadowed"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":60.0,"y":76.0,"w":80.0,"h":30.0,"text":"obj","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":100.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":134.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":76.0,"w":80.0,"h":30.0,"text":"proto","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":220.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":254.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":306.0,"y":76.0,"w":96.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Object.prototype","tone":"yellow","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e3","x1":306.0,"y1":94.0,"x2":306.0,"y2":124.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":306.0,"y":138.0,"w":50.0,"h":22.0,"text":"null","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":60.0,"y":76.0,"w":80.0,"h":30.0,"text":"obj","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":100.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":134.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":76.0,"w":80.0,"h":30.0,"text":"proto","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":220.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":254.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":306.0,"y":76.0,"w":96.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Object.prototype","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":130.0,"text":"obj.toString() → found here","size":9.5,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["const base = { n: 1 };","const o = Object.create(base);","o.n         // 1 — from base","o.n = 5;    // write to o","base.n      // 1 — unchanged"],"hl":[3,4],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":20.0,"w":330.0}]],"cues":[16.5,24.4]}]},{"title":"Constructor and new","sub":"Four steps","short":"new","main":"new creates an object, links the prototype, calls the function and returns the object.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Constructor","What new does","instanceof"],"captions":["Before classes, constructor functions made objects; methods went into the prototype field","new makes an empty object, links its prototype, calls the function with this, returns the object","instanceof checks if the constructor's prototype is in the chain; a forgotten new is common"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["function User(name) {","  this.name = name;","}","User.prototype.hi = function () {","  return 'Hello, ' + this.name;","};"],"hl":[3],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":18.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"s0","x":180.0,"y":34.0,"w":200.0,"h":26.0,"text":"1. empty object","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s1","x":180.0,"y":68.0,"w":200.0,"h":26.0,"text":"2. link prototype","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s2","x":180.0,"y":102.0,"w":200.0,"h":26.0,"text":"3. call with this","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s3","x":180.0,"y":136.0,"w":200.0,"h":26.0,"text":"4. return object","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["const u = new User('Ada');","u instanceof User    // true","u instanceof Object  // true","User('B')  // without new → error"],"hl":[1,2],"bad":[3],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":20.0,"w":310.0}]],"cues":[19.4,27.4]}]},{"title":"Class","sub":"Sugar over prototypes","short":"class","main":"A class is a constructor function; you cannot call it without new.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Class","It is a function","Not hoisted"],"captions":["A class has a constructor and methods; methods go into the prototype and are not enumerable","typeof a class is \"function\": a class is a constructor function; no calling without new","A class is not hoisted: declare it before use; the class body is always in strict mode"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["class Point {","  constructor(x, y) {","    this.x = x; this.y = y;","  }","  len() { return Math.hypot(this.x, this.y); }","}"],"hl":[4],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":18.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["typeof Point           // 'function'","Point(1, 2)","// TypeError: Class constructor","//   Point cannot be invoked without 'new'"],"hl":[1,2],"bad":[1,2],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":20.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["const p = new Point(1, 2);  // ReferenceError","class Point { … }"],"hl":[0],"bad":[0],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":24.0,"w":310.0}]],"cues":[17.2,30.1]}]},{"title":"Fields and privacy","sub":"#private, static, get/set","short":"Fields","main":"A name with a hash sign is a truly private field.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Fields and #private","static","get and set"],"captions":["Fields are declared in the class body; a # name is private: no access, even via [ ]","static makes methods and fields of the class itself, not instances — for factories and counters","Getters and setters look like fields but run code: computed properties and write checks"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["class Acc {","  #balance = 0;","  deposit(x) { this.#balance += x; }","}","new Acc().#balance  // SyntaxError"],"hl":[1],"bad":[4],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":20.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["class Id {","  static next = 1;","  static make() { return Id.next++; }","}","Id.make()   // 1"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":20.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["class Temp {","  #c = 0;","  get f() { return this.#c * 9 / 5 + 32; }","  set c(v) {","    if (v < -273) throw new RangeError();","    this.#c = v;","  }","}"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":15.0,"w":335.0}]],"cues":[10.2,31.2]}]},{"title":"Inheritance","sub":"extends and super","short":"extends","main":"Call super() before the first use of this.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["extends and super","Chain","Custom errors"],"captions":["A child class gets parent methods, overrides them and calls the parent version via super","In a child constructor, call super() before the first access to this","Custom errors extend Error: then instanceof and the call stack work like standard ones"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["class Animal {","  speak() { return '...'; }","}","class Dog extends Animal {","  speak() { return super.speak() + ' woof'; }","}"],"hl":[3,4],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":18.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":90.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Dog.prototype","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":120.0,"y1":90.0,"x2":150.0,"y2":90.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":210.0,"y":90.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Animal.prototype","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":266.0,"y1":90.0,"x2":296.0,"y2":90.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":330.0,"y":90.0,"w":56.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Object","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":140.0,"text":"constructor(): super() before this","size":9.5,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["class HttpError extends Error {","  constructor(status, msg) {","    super(msg);","    this.name = 'HttpError';","    this.status = status;","  }","}"],"hl":[2],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":18.0,"w":330.0}]],"cues":[12.0,30.9]}]},{"title":"Losing this","sub":"bind, arrow, wrapper","short":"this","main":"A method as a callback loses this — bind or wrap it.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["A callback loses this","bind and arrow field","Wrapper"],"captions":["A method passed as a callback loses its object: field access fails with TypeError","Fixes: bind in the constructor or an arrow field — but that is a copy per object","A third way is to wrap the call in an arrow when passing: () => obj.method()"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["button.onclick = timer.tick;","// TypeError: Cannot read properties","//   of undefined (reading 'n')"],"hl":[0],"bad":[1,2],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["constructor() {","  this.tick = this.tick.bind(this);","}","// or a field:","tick = () => { this.n++; };"],"hl":[1,4],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":20.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["button.onclick = () => timer.tick();","setTimeout(() => timer.tick(), 0);"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":24.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[16.1,27.1]}]},{"title":"Composition","sub":"Instead of deep hierarchies","short":"Composition","main":"Build objects from abilities, not from long chains.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Deep hierarchy","Composition","Mixing in"],"captions":["Deep hierarchies are fragile: a change in the parent breaks the descendants","Better to build an object from abilities: \"can fly\", \"can swim\" as separate functions","Mix in with Object.assign or spread; in JavaScript what matters is having the method, not the ancestor"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":30.0,"w":100.0,"h":24.0,"text":"Animal","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":66.0,"w":100.0,"h":24.0,"text":"Bird","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":180.0,"y":102.0,"w":100.0,"h":24.0,"text":"Penguin","tone":"red","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":180.0,"y1":54.0,"x2":180.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":180.0,"y1":90.0,"x2":180.0,"y2":96.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":148.0,"text":"a penguin that \"flies\"?","tone":"red","size":9.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"f","x":80.0,"y":60.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"canFly","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":80.0,"y":100.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"canSwim","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":290.0,"y":80.0,"w":100.0,"h":36.0,"text":"penguin","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":130.0,"y1":66.0,"x2":238.0,"y2":74.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":130.0,"y1":100.0,"x2":238.0,"y2":88.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["const canSwim = { swim() { … } };","const penguin = {","  ...canSwim, walk() { … },","};","penguin.swim?.()"],"hl":[2,4],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":20.0,"w":330.0}]],"cues":[16.1,27.8]}]},{"title":"Descriptors","sub":"writable, enumerable, freeze","short":"Descriptors","main":"freeze and seal protect an object; freezing is shallow.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Three flags","defineProperty","freeze and seal"],"captions":["Each property has flags: writable — writing, enumerable — seen in loops, configurable — deleting","Object.defineProperty sets flags by hand, getOwnPropertyDescriptor shows them","freeze forbids writing and deleting, seal seals the property set, preventExtensions only forbids adding"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"w","x":70.0,"y":76.0,"w":100.0,"h":36.0,"text":"writable\nwrite","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"e","x":180.0,"y":76.0,"w":100.0,"h":36.0,"text":"enumerable\nin loops","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":290.0,"y":76.0,"w":100.0,"h":36.0,"text":"configurable\ndelete","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["Object.defineProperty(o, 'id', {","  value: 7,","  writable: false,","  enumerable: false,","});","o.id = 9;   // silently ignored"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":18.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":56.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"preventExtensions","tone":"blue","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":56.0,"w":80.0,"h":26.0,"text":"seal","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":290.0,"y":56.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"freeze","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t1","x":70.0,"y":90.0,"text":"no\nadding","size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"text":"+ no\ndeleting","size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t3","x":290.0,"y":90.0,"text":"+ no\nchanging","size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":140.0,"text":"freezing is shallow","tone":"yellow","size":9.5}]],"cues":[13.4,31.3]}]},{"title":"Symbols and protocols","sub":"Symbol.iterator","short":"Symbols","main":"A protocol is a method with a special symbol as its key.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Symbol","Well-known symbols","Protocol"],"captions":["A symbol is a unique value; as a key it never clashes with any string name","Built-in symbols — Symbol.iterator, Symbol.toPrimitive, Symbol.toStringTag — drive language behavior","An object with a Symbol.iterator method works in for…of, spread, destructuring and Array.from"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["const id = Symbol('id');","const o = { [id]: 1, id: 2 };","Symbol('id') === Symbol('id')  // false"],"hl":[2],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["obj[Symbol.iterator]     // iteration","obj[Symbol.toPrimitive]   // conversion","obj[Symbol.toStringTag]   // label"],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":80.0,"y":76.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"your object\n[Symbol.iterator]","tone":"yellow","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":130.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":196.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"u0","x":270.0,"y":38.0,"w":100.0,"h":24.0,"text":"for…of","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"u1","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":24.0,"text":"[...x]","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"u2","x":270.0,"y":102.0,"w":100.0,"h":24.0,"text":"Array.from","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"u3","x":270.0,"y":134.0,"w":100.0,"h":24.0,"text":"[a, b] = x","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[15.1,32.1]}]},{"title":"Iterators","sub":"next() and done","short":"Iterators","main":"An iterator is lazy: the next element is computed on request.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["next()","Manual iterator","Laziness"],"captions":["An iterator is an object with next() returning { value, done }; done: true means the end","for…of calls next() again and again; your own iterator must keep state","Elements are computed on demand, so an infinite sequence is possible; break calls return()"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":36.0,"w":230.0,"h":28.0,"text":"{ value: 1, done: false }","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":76.0,"w":230.0,"h":28.0,"text":"{ value: 2, done: false }","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":116.0,"w":230.0,"h":28.0,"text":"{ value: undefined, done: true }","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t","x":60.0,"y":76.0,"text":"next()","size":10.0,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["const range = {","  from: 1, to: 3,","  [Symbol.iterator]() {","    let n = this.from, to = this.to;","    return { next: () =>","      n <= to ? { value: n++, done: false }","              : { value: undefined, done: true } };","  },","};"],"hl":[2,4],"lang":"js","size":8.5,"lh":15.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["for (const x of naturals()) {","  if (x > 3) break;   // calls return()","  console.log(x);","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":310.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":140.0,"text":"an infinite sequence is no problem","size":9.5}]],"cues":[17.1,27.1]}]},{"title":"Generators","sub":"function* and yield","short":"Generators","main":"A generator pauses at yield and resumes from the same place.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["function*","yield","yield*"],"captions":["A function with a star does not run when called but returns a generator object","Each yield pauses and hands out a value; the next next() resumes from the same place","yield* delegates iteration to another iterable; async functions are built on generators too"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["function* gen() {","  yield 1;","  yield 2;","}","const g = gen();   // nothing has run yet"],"hl":[0,4],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":20.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["function* fib() {","  let [a, b] = [0, 1];","  while (true) {","    yield a;","    [a, b] = [b, a + b];","  }","}","[...take(fib(), 6)]  // 0 1 1 2 3 5"],"hl":[3],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":18.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["function* walk(t) {","  if (!t) return;","  yield* walk(t.left);","  yield t.value;","  yield* walk(t.right);","}"],"hl":[2,4],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":20.0,"w":310.0}]],"cues":[10.8,28.5]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"What's next","short":"Summary","main":"Next: asynchrony — the event loop, promises, async and await.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Classes","Iterators","Next"],"captions":["Every object links to a prototype; a class is a constructor and prototype; # fields, static, get and set","Inheritance is extends and super, but composition is often safer; iterators feed for…of and spread, generators write them briefly","Next: modules and errors, then asynchrony: promises, async and await"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"prototype","tone":"yellow","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":240.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":30.0,"text":"class #field","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":160.0,"y":116.0,"w":190.0,"h":28.0,"text":"this gets lost — bind it","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"extends / super","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":240.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Symbol.iterator","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":160.0,"y":116.0,"w":190.0,"h":28.0,"text":"function* and yield","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":40.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["console.log('1');","setTimeout(() => console.log('2'), 0);","console.log('3');"],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":290.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":140.0,"text":"chapter 9: modules and errors","size":9.5}]],"cues":[14.5,30.7]}]}]}